{"name":"Ibis","hex":"#f4b3c2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Ibis","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Threskiornithidae – certain ibises, now in most of the genera of Threskiornithidae and in a genus of family Ciconiidae of storks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Ibis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ibis","blocks":[{"text":"The ibis are a group of long-legged wading birds in the family Threskiornithidae that inhabit wetlands, forests and plains. \"Ibis\" derives from the Latin and Ancient Greek word for this group of birds. It also occurs in the scientific name of the western cattle egret mistakenly identified in 1757 as being the sacred ibis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Black-headed_Ibis_%28Threskiornis_melanocephalus%29.jpg/330px-Black-headed_Ibis_%28Threskiornis_melanocephalus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibis","wikidata":"Q193833"},{"title":"Ibis (hotel)","blocks":[{"text":"Ibis is a French brand of budget hotels owned by Accor. Created in 1974, Ibis became Accor's \"economy megabrand\" in 2011 with the rebranding of Ibis Styles and Ibis Budget from All Seasons and Etap Hôtel respectively. As of 31 December 2025, there were 1,242 hotels under the Ibis brand, with 154,177 rooms worldwide."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ibis_(hotel)","wikidata":"Q920166"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/N190_w1150.jpg/500px-N190_w1150.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/N190_w1150.jpg/1280px-N190_w1150.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/N190_w1150.jpg/500px-N190_w1150.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig